WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.690
We’ve been using the 2018 iPad Pro since
it came out almost a year and a half ago,

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:06.980
and one thing’s for certain..

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.940
It’s been through a lot!

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.650
So let’s examine the history of this iPad
Pro and how our personal thoughts on it have

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.550
changed as software has evolved and brought
us into 2020.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.580
Now we are expecting a new 2020 iPad Pro within
the next couple of months, which we discuss

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.860
in that video which you can check out after
this one, but I personally believe the 2018

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.770
model is gonna sell like hotcakes even after
the 2020 model comes out….

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.090
Let’s talk about why.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:39.280
There are 5 main features of this iPad Pro
that greatly added to its success and they’re

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.050
also the features that really matter for 2020
and beyond!

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.620
But before I get into those features, I want
to quickly go through how this iPad Pro has

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.460
evolved since release.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:55.469
In my first review of the 2018 iPad Pro, less
than two weeks after release, my thoughts

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:57.059
were mostly negative.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:02.239
I mentioned that it was a mistake for Apple
to market the iPad Pro as a computer replacement

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:04.710
when the software was so limiting.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.290
Even though they added the USB-C port, you
couldn’t connect a flash drive or an external

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.930
storage drive.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:16.860
File imports were limited to photos only using
a SD card adapter, and it forced you to use

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.660
the Photos app to do it.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:23.890
They also added external display support,
but it basically only mirrored your display

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:29.130
so you still had to touch your iPad to control
it because at the time, there was no mouse

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.130
support.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:35.399
The 11” model also had a new aspect ratio
which meant that most apps and games couldn’t

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:40.360
use up the full display until they were updated
to specifically support it.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:46.830
And in terms of performance, even though the
2018 iPad Pro is much faster than the 2017

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:52.520
model, they both felt exactly the same because
there were barely any apps that could utilize

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.829
its full power.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:59.860
So basically, when this iPad Pro was released,
it honestly wasn’t really worth buying.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:05.500
And then came iPadOS, which completely changed
the game.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.620
External drives now work perfectly fine, allowing
you to freely drag and drop files to and from

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.780
the iPad Pro.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:16.860
You can even edit photos and videos directly
off of a drive without having to first import

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.270
it onto your iPads local storage.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:24.540
Not only that, but you can now log onto a
storage server wirelessly using SMB.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.600
We did this ourselves and were able to easily
access the files on our server.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:34.890
Apple updated split-view so that you can now
open two instances of the same app right next

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.890
to each other, making it a whole lot more
useful.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.270
Alongside that, they added new gestures for
text selection and undoing mistakes which

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.200
make it easier to use.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.700
Safari added a new Downloads folder feature,
allowing you to download PDFs and other files

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.650
off the internet and quickly use and edit
them.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.400
Apple even added full keyboard shortcut support
so that using your iPads smart keyboard actually

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.160
felt like using a MacBook.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:05.180
A huge bonus for artists and Apple pencil
users was that the Pencil’s latency was

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:11.860
reduced from 20ms to only 9, which make it
feel even more like a real pencil.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.120
Along with that, Apple finally added mouse
support.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.830
Now while it’s not perfect, and it works
similarly to how touch controls work, allowing

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:23.050
you to set your iPad aside using it with an
external display

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:28.220
Those new iPadOS features changed everything
about the iPad Pro, and it started to make

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:33.330
us question whether it could actually replace
a laptop, so we compared them to last year’s

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.630
base MacBook Air and MacBook Pro.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:40.920
Our conclusion was that for the first time
ever, the iPad Pro actually makes a lot of

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.580
sense to buy compared to a laptop.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.890
It’s got tons of power, an excellent display,
great battery life, great portability, and

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:54.700
it’s actually very functional with the new
iPad OS features, giving you awesome multitasking

00:03:54.700 --> 00:04:00.010
and file management capabilities while also
giving you access to the massive database

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.130
of iOS apps and games.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:08.350
And then came MacOS Catalina, which allowed
users to connect their Mac to their iPad Pro

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:12.650
using the new SideCar feature for things like
art and productivity.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:18.780
So now, here we are in 2020, and the great
news is that since the release of iPadOS,

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:23.000
the 2018 iPad Pro has continued to get better
and better.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:28.230
Now, almost all apps that we’ve tried support
the new aspect ratio perfectly.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:32.440
New apps like the full desktop version of
Photoshop are now available and they do a

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:37.530
great job of supporting the iPad Pro, like
for example, supporting the second generation

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.130
Apple Pencil’s new double-tap feature.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:44.660
We’ve notice that there are more and more
apps and games are now utilizing more of the

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:50.070
iPad Pro’s immense performance, allowing
users to really feel the extra power.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:55.600
Not only that, but there are now more games
that support the iPad Pro’s 120Hz display,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:02.080
like Fortnite, which recently added 120 FPS
support to the 2018 iPad Pro, and let me tell

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.120
you, it works incredibly well.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:08.860
So while it seemed ridiculous at launch that
Apple packed in so much power into this iPad

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:13.980
Pro, we’re actually extremely glad that
they did because it’s still very powerful

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.710
even with the latest apps and games that are
being released.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:23.720
Just recently, Microsoft outlook finally added
the long-awaited side-by-side multitasking

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:28.560
support, so you can have two of the same microsoft
app open side by side.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:33.731
And if you look on Amazon, you’ll see a
bunch of USB-C docks for the iPad Pro, really

00:05:33.731 --> 00:05:37.830
giving users more freedom to connect whatever
devices they’d like to.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:43.320
Companies like Brydge are now coming out with
iPad Pro keyboards that feature trackpads

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:48.650
to make them more and more like actual MacBooks,
and if Apple decides to add cursor support

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:53.940
to a future iPadOS update, these new keyboards
will be incredibly useful.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:58.389
Now that we know how drastically the iPad
Pro has evolved since its release, let’s

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:03.100
get into the 5 main features that I think
really matter for 2020 and beyond.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:08.360
First off, the main feature that really sets
the 2018 iPad Pro apart is the design.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:13.240
The square-edges and slate shape make it really
unique compared to any other iPad.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:18.460
It’s also the only iPad to get rid of the
home button and switch to Face ID, giving

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.900
us a display with even bezels and rounded
corners.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:27.720
This makes using this iPad Pro a whole different
experience compared to using any other iPad,

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.690
and that is what really matters going into
2020.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:36.080
And if the rumors are true of the 2020 iPhones
coming with a new square-edged design, the

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:41.320
2018 iPad Pro is going to feel perfectly at
home and not outdated at all.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:45.200
The second main feature that really matters
is the performance.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:49.970
Even though the new iPhone 11 Pro is using
the latest Apple chip, it’s actually still

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:54.051
slower than the iPad Pro in both processor
and graphics performance.

00:06:54.051 --> 00:06:59.810
The performance is so high that even after
a year and a half, it can easily chew through

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:05.870
any app or game on the app store without any
performance issues, so that gives us consumers

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:11.680
a lot of confidence going into 2020, knowing
that we can truly rely on this iPad Pro.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.210
The third main feature is the display.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:19.180
While most of the new higher-end iPads come
with the same Retina quality displays, very

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:24.310
low reflectivity and excellent touch support,
the iPad Pro gets a major advantage.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:30.160
And I’m not talking about the brighter 600
nit display compared to 500 on the others,

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.350
but I’m talking about the fact that the
iPad Pro gets the incredible 120hz ProMotion

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.350
technology.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:41.000
This basically means that the display can
dynamically adjust it’s own refresh rate

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:45.940
between 24hz and 120hz based on the content
you’re viewing.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:51.290
So if you’re watching a movie, the display
refreshes at 24hz which will save battery

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.290
life.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.550
And if you’re on the home screen or playing
a game with 120FPS support, you’re getting

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:03.130
super fluid animations that you just can’t
get on any other iPad, tablet, or even MacBook!

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:08.440
And seeing as more apps and games are starting
to support 120FPS, this ProMotion feature

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:12.750
is going to get even better going into 2020
and beyond!

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:15.770
Now the fourth feature is actually the USB-C
port.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:21.430
Unlike any other iPad, the 2018 iPad Pro is
able to easily connect to an external display

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:27.460
using USB-C. You can also buy a USB-C dock
and get access to a bunch of ports that you

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.130
can’t get on a regular iPad.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:33.969
And what’s special about USB-C is that it’s
able to supply power to external flash drives

00:08:33.969 --> 00:08:39.140
and storage drives, allowing you to easily
transfer files, which is much more complicated

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:41.350
on a Lightning-packing iPad.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:47.600
Having this USB-C port makes this 2018 iPad
Pro much more capable going into 2020, and

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:52.070
it’s gonna allow it to compete with the
upcoming iPad Pro refresh much easier than

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.029
if it was still packing a Lightning port.

00:08:54.029 --> 00:08:59.040
Now, finally onto the 5th main feature, which
admittedly, isn’t really a feature..

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.150
But it’s still a big deal, and that’s
the price!

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:07.580
We’ve seen this iPad Pro go as low as $675
on Amazon.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:11.260
That’s a whole $125 off retail price.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:15.230
And in a couple of months when the new model
comes out, there’s a possibility that it

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:21.370
could drop even lower, maybe as low as 600-625
dollars brand new.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.070
And at that price, you’re seriously getting
so much bang for your buck.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:29.690
We’re talking an iPad that’s so good that
it competes with laptops, so I can imagine

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:36.450
every 2018 iPad Pro getting snatched up off
Amazon as the new 2020 model comes out, because

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:40.650
it’s still going to be that good, going
into 2020 and beyond.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:46.240
So there you guys have it, that’s our review
of the 2018 iPad Pro in 2020.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:51.130
If you enjoyed this video, you guys check
out our video of the iPad Pro playing Fortnite

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:55.190
at 120 frames per second, and if you’re
not already subscribed, you can click that

00:09:55.190 --> 00:10:00.260
circle above so you don’t miss out on our
2020 iPad Pro coverage when it gets released.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:09.040
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next one!

